233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 208 0 R
/E (Access control is a security mechanism that restricts access to resources based on the identity of users or devices. It enforces policies that determine who can perform what actions on which resources. Effective access control ensures that only authorized users can access sensitive information or perform critical functions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 208 0 R
/E (Access control is like having a security guard at a building who checks if people are allowed to enter certain areas. In websites and applications, it's the system that makes sure users can only access what they're supposed to.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
